message: "If you use Kern, its reference implementation, its consensus design or any derivative work, please cite it as below and retain the NOTICE file (Apache License 2.0, Section 4(d))."
title: "Kern: a Layer-1 settlement and registry protocol with the Skald contract language (reference implementation)"
abstract: "Kern is a Layer-1 blockchain protocol designed for institutional legibility: a narrow base layer that settles, governs, attests and registers, and pushes general execution out to optimistic EVM rollups. This is its reference implementation in Python: Tenderbake-style BFT consensus with a Tendermint lock and valid round, a persistent signing journal and proposal equivocation evidence; bonded Proof-of-Stake delegation with slashing; the Skald contract language, whose declared invariants the runtime enforces; slashable generic attestations; dual-track on-chain governance; the Heimdall explorer; and a one-command multi-node devnet in Docker. The release candidate is pre-audit: consensus safety is validated on a network simulator, on real node processes and on a containerized devnet, but not yet on a network of independent operators, and it has not been professionally audited."
type: software
